Synopsis:
In a frantic and comedic mood, a llama slips on a frozen pond while reaching for berries and gets its tongue stuck, while a little penguin eats the remaining berry and then stands on railroad tracks holding another berry as a steam locomotive barrels toward it. After the train speeds past, the llama catches the berry on its tongue while an adult penguin makes a threatening gesture from behind the rail, and the little penguin leaps off the llama to grab the berry just before wooden planks collapse beneath both of them. Awakening in an underground cavern, they reach for a hanging bunch of berries from a precarious minecart and plunge in terror down steep subterranean tracks, crashing through scaffolding before bursting out of a mountain exit that catapults the llama and the berries into the sky. As the llama eagerly reaches for the floating berries in mid-air, the adult penguin grabs onto its back while the little penguin tumbles nearby, and they plummet and bounce onto the snowy mountain peaks below. The little penguin slides down the slope toward its distant colony, leaving the injured llama crying alone on a rocky ledge until nightfall, when the little penguin and the adult penguins return carrying branches of berries to share a happy meal together by a lighthouse.